{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The town of Hamlet has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people for each horse, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sheep for each cow, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ducks for each person. Which of the following could not possibly be the total number of people, horses, sheep, cows, and ducks in Hamlet?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be694b17d773ff11ab43b01d40f408909b5e4e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }41\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }47\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }59\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }61\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the amount of people be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, horses be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, sheep be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, cows be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and ducks be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \nWe know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec9caac505df773ceb3647f5e311ba8f92e07cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3p=h\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481f33f8826a3655d4e42927cae977027388206b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4s=c\\]\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43f3ef835d562db6c6473375929a629c00732ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3d=p\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> Then the total amount of people, horses, sheep, cows, and ducks may be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c36fd87fd956656251c0d7867c8c6619fee4e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+h+s+c+d = 3d+3(3d)+s+4s+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"345\" height=\"20\" />. This is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db7dd293512fe264bbc465880dab3bbe14eefcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13d+5s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />. Looking through the options, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is impossible to make for integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24344a968d5974e1b4ec714736412a3405afa010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 47}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Intuitive)\">Solution 2 (Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As the solution above says, the total amount of people, horses, sheep, cows, and ducks may be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db7dd293512fe264bbc465880dab3bbe14eefcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13d+5s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />. However, instead of going through each of the solutions and testing the options, you can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chicken_McNugget_Theorem\" title=\"Chicken McNugget Theorem\">Chicken McNugget Theorem</a> to find the greatest number of people, horses, sheep, cows, and ducks that cannot be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db7dd293512fe264bbc465880dab3bbe14eefcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13d+5s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3cc9ce8306192c97c0dee56b766eabe800d4efb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[13\\cdot 5-13-5=47,\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24344a968d5974e1b4ec714736412a3405afa010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 47}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Kflsqi21yZc\">https://youtu.be/Kflsqi21yZc</a>\n</p><p>~Dolphin James Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SOH98fsk-9c\">https://youtu.be/SOH98fsk-9c</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B\">2015 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n<